{"edits": [], "notes": "No edits proposed. Every original finding (models/models.py:36, 37, 39, 52, 60, 70, 74, 92, 107, 141) is already fixed in the current content: name/email have `= None` defaults, the root_validator is now `@model_validator(mode="before")` with `@classmethod`, both `class Config` blocks are replaced by `model_config = ConfigDict(populate_by_name=True)`, and all `@validator` uses are now `@field_validator` with `mode="before"` where `pre=True` was used. Re-applying or undoing any of these would be wrong.

The reported failure does not appear to come from this file. It is a `keycloak.exceptions.KeycloakConnectionError` from urllib3 ("Connection refused" to localhost:35789) raised while requesting a token in test_teams_client_no_connection_proxy. Nothing in models/models.py makes network calls or raises that error, and the traceback shows no pydantic validation error. The fix belongs in the keycloak client/test setup (for example, the test expecting a connection failure to be wrapped or handled differently, or the test environment lacking a mock server), not in the model definitions. I did not change the test or client code since they are outside the listed files.

Possible follow-up (not a v1 deprecation, so not proposed): Team.clean_attributes calls `v.items()` in a mode="before" validator, so passing `attributes=None` raises AttributeError rather than a ValidationError. Pydantic v2 only converts ValueError/AssertionError into validation errors, so this is worth a guard if None is a valid input, but it is a behavior question and was left unchanged to avoid altering behavior."}
